laurel 2153: the GPU zap shader no longer hangs the GPU start (boot 2026-11-01 05:52:41: 'TopazGPU: zap: metadata at 0xc0000000', then nothing for > 4 min, no CPU busy, CPU renderer after 68 s). Cause: TopazAdreno.cpp had its own smc()/scm() without the kernel's TrustZone lock (laurel 2404 added one lock to TopazModem's scm() for the modem and ADSP PAS; TopazAdreno was missed). Its PIL_SHUTDOWN/PIL_INIT_IMAGE for PAS 13 entered TrustZone from a second CPU while the modem's auth_and_reset was between two of its 35 interrupted resumes; that call never returned. Fix in the zap path only: (1) every GPU SCM call goes through topaz_scm() (TopazModem: one lock over the call and its resume loop, SCM_V2_EBUSY retried 100 x 30 ms, as downstream scm.c scm_lock / mainline qcom_scm_lock); the local smc() is removed. (2) No PAS_SHUTDOWN before init_image (nothing loaded PAS 13 in this boot; Linux pil-tz and mainline adreno zap_shader_load_mdt do not either); PAS_SHUTDOWN only after init_image succeeded and a later step failed (Linux pil_deinit_image_trusted). (3) Self-check: PAS_IS_SUPPORTED(13) first; a failed call (x0 != 0) turns the GPU off at once with 'LAUREL GPU: off: zap shader failed: TrustZone has no PIL call for PAS 13 ...' (x1 is not a gate: this TZ answers 0 for the modem's PAS 4, which loads). (4) The metadata goes into the TopazModem pool (0xE0000000-0xE1000000, where TrustZone read the ADSP and modem metadata in the same boot); the GPU pool (0xC0000000) only when that pool is off. (5) Each SCM step logs its time in ms.

